# DIAGNOSTICS

devmgr prints to the log what it found, `devmgr: <n> PCI functions, <n> ACPI devices, <n> IOMMUs; <n> to bind`, and `devmgr: bound <n>` when it is done, and why any driver could not be started.
An error that stops it begins `devmgr:`.

# BUGS

Only PCI segment 0 is read.
A function's interrupt is routed only if it is on the root bus; one behind a bridge has none.
A function gets one MSI vector.
An ACPI device gets six ranges at most, its own and its linked ones together.
A power resource another device also names is turned off with either; nothing counts its users.

The IOMMUs: VT-d devices behind bridges, AMD-Vi exclusion ranges and SMMUv1 and v2 are not handled, and a device they would cover has no BTI on an IOMMU.
